1
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,600
OK, Richard. That's terrific.

2
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,000
Your pressure is 120 over 75, and that's fine.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:35,100
Now stand up, please.

4
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:39,200
Good, it's 122 over 80.

5
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:43,300
You can sit down now.

6
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,849
When was your last complete physical?

7
00:00:45,849 --> 00:00:47,100
Six months ago.

8
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,900
Good. Do you have any back or knee problems?

9
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,800
Nope. I am in perfect health.

10
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,157
What do you do for a living, Mr. Stewart?

11
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:54,394
I'm a photographer.

12
00:00:54,394 --> 00:00:57,000
Interesting. What do you photograph?

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,600
Everything. The American scene. People, places, events.

14
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:05,600
Did you ever think of photographing an aerobics class?

15
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:09,900
No...I can't remember taking pictures of people exercising.

16
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,600
But don't you think it'd be a good subject?

17
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,200
Sure.

18
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,000
I need some good photos for my advertising, Mr. Stewart.

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,146
Maybe you can photogragh a class,

20
00:01:19,146 --> 00:01:20,957
and I can give you and Mrs.Stewart

21
00:01:20,957 --> 00:01:22,595
a month of classes ree.

22
00:01:22,595 --> 00:01:24,069
When can I photograph a class?

23
00:01:24,069 --> 00:01:25,917
Anytime.

24
00:01:25,917 --> 00:01:26,845
How about today?

25
00:01:26,845 --> 00:01:30,500
Terrific!

26
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,200
Hi.

27
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:36,100
Oh, hi.

28
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:36,300
Are we ready to go?

29
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:37,100
Yeah. Yeah. Let's get in our lines.

30
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:40,000
We're going to take it slow first.

31
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,900
Stretch up...and we're going to go left first ...

32
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:53,400
2,3,4 ... now switch. ...

33
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,364
OK, hold to the right.

34
00:01:55,364 --> 00:02:02,800
Sunrises. Stretch it out. Flat back.

35
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:15,800
Bring it up ... and twists ... and side ... 2, 3 ...

36
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:23,400
and left ... push ... push ... turn ... hit the floor.

37
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:37,100
Take it side again .... OK, and switch. Stretch it out.

38
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:39,700
And we're going to warm down with a tango.

39
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:56,300
Left, right. Enjoy it.

40
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:58,800
Richard, did you go to the Davis Aerobics class today?

41
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:03,860
Yes, I went to the aerobics class today.

42
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:06,600
What is wrong with you?

43
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,700
Nothing. I am in excellent health.

44
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,000
I have ideal blood pressure. A perfect heart.

45
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,900
In other words, I'm in wonderful condition.

46
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:18,900
Richard, did you go to the aerobics class, really?

47
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:22,500
And don't forget to invite Susan for dinner.

48
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,116
And your legs don't hurt?

49
00:03:24,116 --> 00:03:27,100
Hurt? What do you mean?

50
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:31,100
What about your arms? Lift your arms up like this.

51
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:34,955
And they don't hurt ot even a little?

52
00:03:34,955 --> 00:03:38,877
Nope.

53
00:03:38,877 --> 00:03:41,877
You are in great condition. I can't believe it!
